1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,870
Hamburgers, egg pancakes, sizzling noodles

2
00:00:02,870 --> 00:00:05,606
Rice balls, toast, and savory soy milk

3
00:00:05,606 --> 00:00:08,809
There are so many delicious breakfasts
around the world

4
00:00:08,809 --> 00:00:13,347
I'm going to collect them all in my
breakfast truck

5
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:14,214
And so,

6
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:15,749
Beelu, who loves breakfast,

7
00:00:15,749 --> 00:00:18,619
set off on an adventure to collect

8
00:00:18,619 --> 00:00:21,021
all kinds of breakfast!

9
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,458
That was fun!

10
00:01:00,127 --> 00:01:02,129
Let's find breakfast!

11
00:01:02,129 --> 00:01:04,731
Good morning, Beelu! Good morning, kids!

12
00:01:04,731 --> 00:01:07,467
Today's breakfast is jam toast

13
00:01:07,467 --> 00:01:09,403
In the adventure story coming up,

14
00:01:09,403 --> 00:01:12,272
there will be three jam toast stickers

15
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:13,740
Help Beelu

16
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,143
find where they are!

17
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:18,345
Let's collect today's breakfast!

18
00:01:25,218 --> 00:01:26,820
Good morning, everyone!

19
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:28,488
I'm so excited!

20
00:01:28,488 --> 00:01:30,090
Today is the final day

21
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,292
of the Delicious Toast Breakfast Shop
Contest

22
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:34,695
The toast shop that earns five stars

23
00:01:34,695 --> 00:01:36,229
will receive sponsorship

24
00:01:36,229 --> 00:01:40,033
and be able to open many branches around
the world

25
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:41,635
Everyone holding a star,

26
00:01:41,635 --> 00:01:44,838
don't forget to find your favorite toast
shop

27
00:01:44,838 --> 00:01:47,040
and give them your star!

28
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:52,446
Where is the best toast breakfast shop?

29
00:01:54,648 --> 00:01:57,050
Would you like some breakfast, student?

30
00:01:57,584 --> 00:01:59,386
Come on, come on! This way, please!

31
00:01:59,386 --> 00:02:01,188
An unworthy customer like you

32
00:02:01,188 --> 00:02:03,857
belongs at my distinguished shop!

33
00:02:06,393 --> 00:02:07,995
Which shop should I choose?

34
00:02:09,596 --> 00:02:10,731
Look, customer!

35
00:02:10,731 --> 00:02:12,466
My shop has four stars

36
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,801
Just one more star and I'll...

37
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:17,004
Hey! My star!

38
00:02:17,004 --> 00:02:18,939
Wow, it flew so far!

39
00:02:18,939 --> 00:02:21,208
How did it turn into a shooting star?

40
00:02:22,609 --> 00:02:24,478
Don't mind him, student

41
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:27,547
Come try my special strawberry toast

42
00:02:27,547 --> 00:02:29,149
Come on, come on, come on, come on!

43
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:31,218
Oh, all right

44
00:02:34,421 --> 00:02:36,089
Here, please enjoy

45
00:02:36,089 --> 00:02:39,693
Wow, I'm going to dig in!

46
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:45,832
It's so delicious!

47
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:50,704
Right, student?

48
00:02:50,704 --> 00:02:53,840
My strawberry toast already has four stars

49
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:56,176
All I need is your one star

50
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:59,246
and I'll get five stars before

51
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:02,249
that weird bat next door

52
00:03:02,249 --> 00:03:05,519
Please give me your star!

53
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:07,721
Please, please, please, please!

54
00:03:07,721 --> 00:03:10,524
You're the one who doesn't deserve that
precious star!

55
00:03:17,731 --> 00:03:22,002
Looks like the faucet in your shop is
broken

56
00:03:22,002 --> 00:03:24,604
You actually resorted to that trick!

57
00:03:24,604 --> 00:03:26,807
I don't know what you're talking about

58
00:03:26,807 --> 00:03:29,009
Come this way, customer

59
00:03:29,009 --> 00:03:29,810
Please

60
00:03:32,279 --> 00:03:33,213
My shop

61
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:36,283
isn't as noisy as that bear's shop across
the street

62
00:03:36,283 --> 00:03:37,350
Come

63
00:03:38,685 --> 00:03:39,686
You, honored guest,

64
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:42,756
will surely love our chocolate toast

65
00:03:49,496 --> 00:03:50,964
Tasty!

66
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:54,835
It's delicious, isn't it?

67
00:03:54,835 --> 00:03:55,969
So...

68
00:03:55,969 --> 00:03:58,839
I'll be taking your one star, customer

69
00:03:58,839 --> 00:04:00,440
That's not going to happen!

70
00:04:01,374 --> 00:04:03,510
Of course my toast is better

71
00:04:03,510 --> 00:04:05,045
Mine is better!

72
00:04:09,649 --> 00:04:12,786
Customer, which toast do you think tastes
better?

73
00:04:13,787 --> 00:04:16,256
I think they're both delicious

74
00:04:16,256 --> 00:04:18,058
I can't choose!

75
00:04:19,793 --> 00:04:20,660
What?

76
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,262
How can that mud-like sauce

77
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:23,730
taste good?

78
00:04:23,730 --> 00:04:26,333
Mud belongs on the ground!

79
00:04:31,204 --> 00:04:33,940
Do you know how much effort

80
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:36,343
I've put into my chocolate sauce?

81
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:42,015
You started this war!

82
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:54,161
My strawberry jam!

83
00:04:56,163 --> 00:04:56,897
You're going too far!

84
00:04:57,030 --> 00:04:58,431
You're going too far!

85
00:05:00,901 --> 00:05:03,904
You two, don't fight!

86
00:05:03,904 --> 00:05:05,172
Wait!

87
00:05:22,055 --> 00:05:23,657
Fully armed!

88
00:05:24,257 --> 00:05:25,859
Ladies and gentlemen!

89
00:05:25,859 --> 00:05:28,195
Bomber mode!

90
00:05:34,067 --> 00:05:36,603
Counterattack! Charge!

91
00:05:46,413 --> 00:05:48,014
Don't go too far!

92
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:50,083
Your chocolate tree was the one that

93
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:52,285
kept my strawberries from getting sunlight

94
00:05:52,285 --> 00:05:53,820
You're no better!

95
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:55,222
One time, you used up all the water

96
00:05:55,222 --> 00:05:56,690
and left me with none

97
00:06:09,236 --> 00:06:11,104
Let go! Let go!

98
00:06:14,708 --> 00:06:16,910
This can't go on!

99
00:06:17,444 --> 00:06:20,180
Let's do the Breakfast Brain Workout

100
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,649
and find a way to end this war!

101
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:41,534
It's Brain Workout Time!

102
00:06:41,534 --> 00:06:45,272
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

103
00:06:45,272 --> 00:06:47,073
Clap! Clap!

104
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,942
Jump up!

105
00:06:48,942 --> 00:06:52,746
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

106
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:54,748
Clap! Clap!

107
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:55,015
Jump up!

108
00:06:55,148 --> 00:06:56,416
Jump up!

109
00:06:56,416 --> 00:07:00,153
Make a sun with your hands and say good
morning

110
00:07:00,153 --> 00:07:02,489
Clap! Clap!

111
00:07:02,489 --> 00:07:05,091
Bi Ru Akokay

112
00:07:07,027 --> 00:07:10,230
Oh, I've got a great idea!

113
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,032
To stop you two from fighting,

114
00:07:12,032 --> 00:07:14,100
the best way is to...

115
00:07:23,843 --> 00:07:26,646
Don't worry, the sunshine is here!

116
00:07:27,314 --> 00:07:30,183
You'll become the best strawberry jam!

117
00:07:32,652 --> 00:07:33,653
Hang in there!

118
00:07:33,653 --> 00:07:35,455
I'll water you right away

119
00:07:36,656 --> 00:07:39,392
You have to become the tastiest chocolate
sauce!

120
00:07:42,195 --> 00:07:43,997
So he also...

121
00:07:43,997 --> 00:07:46,866
loves his own jam toast this much?

122
00:07:54,874 --> 00:07:58,345
Oh no! What have I done?

123
00:07:58,345 --> 00:08:00,880
We actually did all this over

124
00:08:00,880 --> 00:08:03,016
one star, ruining each other's hard work

125
00:08:09,756 --> 00:08:10,824
I'm sorry

126
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:13,693
Our argument dragged you into this

127
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:17,097
It's okay. I'm Beelu

128
00:08:17,097 --> 00:08:19,366
I still don't know your names

129
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:21,701
I'm Ah-He

130
00:08:21,701 --> 00:08:23,103
I'm Ping-Ping

131
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:29,242
Neither of us deserves this star

132
00:08:36,116 --> 00:08:38,251
We'll make breakfast for you

133
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,804
As expected, they're both delicious!

134
00:08:57,804 --> 00:08:59,606
I can't pick a winner!

135
00:09:00,807 --> 00:09:02,008
Next time you come,

136
00:09:02,008 --> 00:09:05,078
I'll make even better strawberry toast

137
00:09:05,078 --> 00:09:07,680
My chocolate toast won't lose either!

138
00:09:15,822 --> 00:09:17,957
That was fun!

139
00:09:23,296 --> 00:09:25,098
Let's find breakfast!

140
00:09:25,098 --> 00:09:26,833
Here are the answers!

141
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:29,502
Today's breakfast stickers are in these
places

142
00:09:33,506 --> 00:09:34,908
Did you find them?

143
00:09:38,044 --> 00:09:40,380
Yeah, I knew it!

144
00:09:42,382 --> 00:09:44,584
How do you make delicious jam toast?

145
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:45,452
First,

146
00:09:45,452 --> 00:09:46,519
knead the flour and seasonings

147
00:09:46,519 --> 00:09:48,321
with the yeast to make a dough

148
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,257
Let it rise

149
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:52,725
Then cut it into small pieces

150
00:09:52,725 --> 00:09:53,927
Let it rise again

151
00:09:54,727 --> 00:09:55,862
When the time is right,

152
00:09:55,862 --> 00:09:57,597
roll the dough out evenly

153
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,465
Roll it up

154
00:09:59,199 --> 00:10:00,733
Then put it into a baking pan

155
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:02,402
Wait for the final proof

156
00:10:04,404 --> 00:10:06,806
Then put it in the oven to bake

157
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:10,343
Once baked, remove it from the pan and
slice it

158
00:10:11,077 --> 00:10:12,612
Toast the slices again

159
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:14,747
Spread on the jam

160
00:10:14,747 --> 00:10:17,217
And delicious jam toast is ready!

161
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,020
Wow, it looks delicious!

162
00:10:25,492 --> 00:10:28,294
Why, when you look closely at a slice of
toast,

163
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:31,164
do you see lots of little holes?

164
00:10:33,099 --> 00:10:36,503
That's because when toast is made,

165
00:10:36,503 --> 00:10:38,438
yeast is added to the dough

166
00:10:38,438 --> 00:10:39,706
Yeast?

167
00:10:39,706 --> 00:10:40,707
That's right

168
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:42,642
Yeast is what makes bread

169
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:44,978
fluffy and delicious

170
00:10:45,912 --> 00:10:48,915
When yeast mixes with the dough, it
produces gas

171
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,451
Look

172
00:10:51,451 --> 00:10:53,586
Let the dough rest for a while

173
00:10:53,586 --> 00:10:56,189
and it will rise and get bigger

174
00:10:56,189 --> 00:10:59,058
because it's filled with gas

175
00:10:59,058 --> 00:11:02,462
Wow, the dough really got bigger!

176
00:11:04,264 --> 00:11:05,398
That's right

177
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:08,468
During baking, these gases

178
00:11:08,468 --> 00:11:10,537
expand the air pockets in the dough

179
00:11:10,537 --> 00:11:12,272
and make them bigger and bigger

180
00:11:13,006 --> 00:11:15,875
So when we slice the bread,

181
00:11:15,875 --> 00:11:19,012
we see all those little holes

182
00:11:20,146 --> 00:11:23,016
Oh, I see

183
00:11:23,016 --> 00:11:23,950
Also,

184
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:26,953
don't eat toast immediately after it comes
out of the oven

185
00:11:26,953 --> 00:11:29,289
Because not only is the bread very hot,

186
00:11:29,289 --> 00:11:31,758
it's also full of gas inside

187
00:11:32,425 --> 00:11:34,627
Eating it may make you feel bloated

188
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:38,898
Oh, but after all this explaining,

189
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:41,167
I should be able to eat some toast now,
right?

190
00:11:42,235 --> 00:11:43,303
Yes!

191
00:11:43,303 --> 00:11:44,370
Please dig in!
